| execute_sql {"sql": "CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_payment_customer_id_amount ON payment(customer_id, amount)"}
| execute_sql {"sql": "CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_payment_customer_id_payment_date ON payment(customer_id, payment_date)"}
| execute_sql {"sql": "CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_customer_active ON customer(active)"}
| execute_sql {"sql": "WITH payment_agg AS (\n  SELECT\n    customer_id,\n    COUNT(payment_id) AS total_payments,\n    SUM(amount) AS total_spent,\n    AVG(amount) AS avg_payment,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT EXTRACT(month FROM payment_date)) AS active_months,\n    MAX(payment_date) AS last_payment,\n    MIN(payment_date) AS first_payment,\n    COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE amount > 5.0) AS high_value_payments,\n    SUM(amount) FILTER (WHERE payment_date >= '2007-03-01') AS recent_spending\n  FROM payment\n  GROUP BY customer_id\n)\nSELECT\n  c.customer_id,\n  c.first_name,\n  c.last_name,\n  c.email,\n  pa.total_payments,\n  pa.total_spent,\n  pa.avg_payment,\n  pa.active_months,\n  pa.last_payment,\n  pa.first_payment,\n  pa.high_value_payments,\n  pa.recent_spending\nFROM customer c\nJOIN payment_agg pa ON c.customer_id = pa.customer_id\nWHERE c.active = 1\nAND pa.total_payments >= 10\nORDER BY pa.total_spent DESC, pa.total_payments DESC;"}
| explain_query {"sql": "WITH payment_agg AS (\n  SELECT\n    customer_id,\n    COUNT(payment_id) AS total_payments,\n    SUM(amount) AS total_spent,\n    AVG(amount) AS avg_payment,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT EXTRACT(month FROM payment_date)) AS active_months,\n    MAX(payment_date) AS last_payment,\n    MIN(payment_date) AS first_payment,\n    COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE amount > 5.0) AS high_value_payments,\n    SUM(amount) FILTER (WHERE payment_date >= '2007-03-01') AS recent_spending\n  FROM payment\n  GROUP BY customer_id\n)\nSELECT\n  c.customer_id,\n  c.first_name,\n  c.last_name,\n  c.email,\n  pa.total_payments,\n  pa.total_spent,\n  pa.avg_payment,\n  pa.active_months,\n  pa.last_payment,\n  pa.first_payment,\n  pa.high_value_payments,\n  pa.recent_spending\nFROM customer c\nJOIN payment_agg pa ON c.customer_id = pa.customer_id\nWHERE c.active = 1\nAND pa.total_payments >= 10\nORDER BY pa.total_spent DESC, pa.total_payments DESC;","analyze": true}
Optimization Summary:

1. Created indexes to support filtering and joining on "payment" and "customer" tables:
   - Index on payment(customer_id, amount)
   - Index on payment(customer_id, payment_date)
   - Index on customer(active)

2. Rewrote the original query to remove correlated subqueries:
   - Pre-aggregated all payment metrics (total counts, sums, averages, filtered counts/sums) in a single CTE (payment_agg).
   - Joined customer with the pre-aggregated payment data.
   - Filtered on active customers and minimum payments in the main query.

Performance Improvement:

- Original query execution time was about 1726 ms.
- Optimized query execution time is about 14.6 ms.
- The query plan shows removal of expensive nested subqueries and use of efficient hash join and aggregation.

This optimization drastically reduces runtime by avoiding repeated scans of the "payment" table for each customer and leveraging indexes for faster filtering and joins.

